<title>USA: U.S.'s Shafer says dollar policy unchanged.</title>
<headline>U.S.'s Shafer says dollar policy unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A senior Treasury official on Wednesday reiterated the Clinton administration's support for a strong dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;Our exchange rate policy has not changed,&quot; U.S. Treasury Undersecretary Jeffrey Shafer told reporters. &quot;We're focusing on the fundamentals.&quot;</p>
<p>Shafer made the remarks in response to a question about whether U.S. policy on the dollar had changed.  </p>
<p>Shafer added, &quot;Our policy is to have a strong dollar.&quot;</p>
<p>He stressed that he was repeating U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin's views.</p>
</text>
